<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--

InoSpeakNG — Unreal Plugin Language (UPL) file for Android APK packaging
of espeak-ng.

Referenced from InoSpeakNG.Build.cs via
    AdditionalPropertiesForReceipt.Add("AndroidPlugin", "<this file>")

Two concerns handled here, matching the proven pattern from the
sibling InoLiteRT and InoOnnx plugins' UPL files:

  1. Java-side loadLibrary: emit System.loadLibrary("espeak-ng") in
     the generated GameActivity Java so the .so is resident before
     libUnreal.so runs and consumer modules try to call espeak_*
     symbols.

  2. APK staging: copy libespeak-ng.so from the plugin's
     Source/ThirdParty/Android/<arch>/ into the APK's lib/<arch>/
     directory so Android's dynamic linker finds it.

Both are required. RuntimeDependencies in Build.cs alone does NOT stage
a .so into lib/<arch>/ of the APK — explicit <copyFile> in
<resourceCopies> is what gets it there.

The espeak-ng-data tree (~3 MB of phoneme dictionaries / voice tables)
is NOT staged here — UPL <copyFile> places files into the APK's
assets/, which espeak-ng's raw fopen() can't read. Instead the data
goes in via Build.cs RuntimeDependencies (UFS/pak), and on first run
FInoSpeakNGModule extracts it to FPaths::ProjectPersistentDownloadDir()
so espeak_Initialize can fopen() it as regular files. See
InoSpeakNG.cpp's ExtractEspeakDataIfNeeded.

Path variable gotchas (lessons from sibling plugins' UPLs):

  $S(AbsPluginDir)  — resolves to THIS MODULE's directory:
                       Plugins/InoSpeakNG/Source/InoSpeakNG/
                       (despite the "Plugin" in the name).
  $S(PluginDir)     — does NOT exist as a UPL variable; using it
                       silently produces "" and breaks copies. Always
                       use $S(AbsPluginDir).
  $S(BuildDir)      — Intermediate/Android/<arch>/gradle/app/src/main/
  $S(Architecture)  — arm64-v8a or x86_64.

Our .so files live at
    Plugins/InoSpeakNG/Source/ThirdParty/Android/<arch>/libespeak-ng.so
which is one dir up + over from $S(AbsPluginDir).

We support both arm64-v8a and x86_64. UPL is processed once per
architecture; bSupported is set per-arch via <isArch>, so the
<copyFile> directive only runs for arches we actually built a .so for.

If you only built one arch (e.g. arm64-v8a but not x86_64), the
bSupported gating still runs <copyFile> for the arch UE is currently
packaging. Building x86_64 separately:
    cd Plugins/InoSpeakNG/EspeakNG/scripts
    ./setup-android.ps1 -AndroidAbi x86_64

Docs: https://docs.unrealengine.com/en-US/Sharing/Reference/UnrealPluginLanguage/

-->
<root xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

	<!-- File trace for debugging: UE logs a line whenever this UPL is
	     processed. Useful for confirming the packager picked it up. -->
	<trace enable="true"/>

	<!--
	init: runs once per architecture. Gate the copy on architecture so
	we don't try to copy x86_64 binaries into an arm64-v8a build dir.
	Matches the stock UE UPL pattern.
	-->
	<init>
		<log text="InoSpeakNG UPL init"/>
		<setBool result="bSupported" value="false"/>
		<isArch arch="arm64-v8a">
			<setBool result="bSupported" value="true"/>
		</isArch>
		<isArch arch="x86_64">
			<setBool result="bSupported" value="true"/>
		</isArch>
		<if condition="bSupported">
			<false>
				<log text="InoSpeakNG: unsupported architecture $S(Architecture), skipping native lib staging"/>
			</false>
		</if>
	</init>

	<!--
	soLoadLibrary: emit System.loadLibrary("espeak-ng") in the Java
	launcher activity so libespeak-ng.so is resident before
	FInoSpeakNGModule::StartupModule's espeak_Initialize call runs.

	The Build.cs adds the .so via PublicAdditionalLibraries, which
	gives libUnreal.so a DT_NEEDED on libespeak-ng.so — so technically
	the dynamic linker would load it automatically. We still include
	the explicit soLoadLibrary preload so a load failure surfaces as
	a Java UnsatisfiedLinkError (with our failmsg) rather than a
	silent native abort during libUnreal.so init.

	Java's System.loadLibrary("foo") looks up "libfoo.so" in
	lib/<arch>/ — so the Java-side name is "espeak-ng" (without the
	"lib" prefix and ".so" suffix).
	-->
	<soLoadLibrary>
		<loadLibrary name="espeak-ng" failmsg="Failed to load libespeak-ng.so — ensure EspeakNG/scripts/setup-android.ps1 has been run for this architecture and the APK re-packaged."/>
	</soLoadLibrary>

	<!--
	resourceCopies: copy libespeak-ng.so into the APK's
	lib/$S(Architecture)/ directory. UE's APK packager then ships
	one libs/ subfolder per arch, and the install step on device
	picks the matching arch.

	The src path uses $S(Architecture) so the same UPL works for
	both arm64-v8a and x86_64 packaging passes — UPL re-runs once
	per arch, $S(Architecture) substitutes accordingly, and the
	matching .so under Source/ThirdParty/Android/<arch>/ is picked.

	The <log> line prints to the packaging log so we can verify
	the copy actually ran. Look for "InoSpeakNG: copied libespeak-ng.so"
	in the output.
	-->
	<resourceCopies>
		<if condition="bSupported">
			<true>
				<copyFile
					src="$S(AbsPluginDir)/../ThirdParty/Android/$S(Architecture)/libespeak-ng.so"
					dst="$S(BuildDir)/libs/$S(Architecture)/libespeak-ng.so"/>
				<log text="InoSpeakNG: copied libespeak-ng.so for $S(Architecture)"/>
			</true>
		</if>
	</resourceCopies>

</root>
